# B0-r2: review candidate, no runtime authorization

Fixed source3adc/309 inputs, unchanged workflows15763B SHA6d8a1985;
StageA d852 package930368B SHA2fe071e2,1012 actual emits/1014 full members.
Default80, Node/curl opt-in. No liveHEAD/private/engine/ERE/YQ/XAN inputs.

Preseal tuples are DISTINCT:
- StageA: ab976f5ee31d0a793d6016f13cc46e6960ace2aa:
  tests/integration/agent-bash-coherent-author-20260829/stage-a-r2/PRESEAL.json,
  blob07885258c60b0d2b8b72df21001e3ae79da0ba48,47291B,
  SHA8acc5e35686a4fa20bf1f8a871b2c23edff4cb29b09a9b9f1848ffc1332006db.
- Fixture:955e7eb7d7f49feb4cf288fcb58a6ba6125073f0:
  tests/integration/agent-bash-coherent-author-20260829/v4/PRESEAL.json,
  blobc2fd250aa87370d508156631b3c2305e3e7260ca,8922B,
  SHA4911f32f621e33adf8cacd0eabbc13b0644586fc3efd36ca42abf3c85765734c.

All13 IDs C01–C09,C12,C13,C14,C17 execute once per source-built/installed/moved
layout,39 calls. Every program, explicit cwd/env, expected stdout/status/effects,
registered cleanup and release-finally is in unchanged workflows.mjs. Default
MemoryFS cwd '/', env{}; Git fixture workflows use '/repo'. C17 returns EXACT
invoke Promise, not async/wrapped. Public Shell.exec/dispose method descriptors
are checked in runner; selected shell.js/import closure is package-authenticated.
No new claim about opaque provider finalization, full cleanup or GNU parity.

Regex derivation: scripts invoke true/printf/cat/false, strict flags/basic [[ ]],
LET/source, mock curl, Git reads/diff and apply_patch. No grep/sed/rg/expr-regex
or =~ command is requested. This predicts no application RegexWorker for these
scripts, NOT a measured zero. Retain public80 resources/loader EXACT mechanism:
maximum2 RegexWorkers/layout,6 total,live2; only authenticated regex worker.js
and execArgv[] admitted. Nodeguest Workers fail that entry check. Three fixed
Node --loader admissions (one/layout) are separate internal threads, not counted
as application Workers. Record actual create/exit IDs and beforeExit live0.
Whole static package closure is authenticated pre/post; inherited loader observes
main-thread file loads, NOT new nested-worker import proof. Its next() reread and
host filesystem race limitations remain; immutable owned inputs are assumed.
No stalled comparator instrumented profile is used.

Run proposal: fresh ROOT B0 GO, then launch.sh PRESEAL_PATH SHA BYTES with
B0_ROOT_GO=ROOT_B0_39_EXPLICIT_FRESH_AUTHORIZATION. Bootstrap checks all sealed
source before importing controller. No launch in preparation. launch capture
uses exclusive /private/tmp/coherent-b0-39-20260829-r2.launch.{stdout,stderr}.
Work root /private/tmp/safe-bash-coherent-b0-20260829-r2 must not exist.

Controller roles: authenticated StageA supervisor common.mjs; one npm offline
install child, three sequential consumer children. Retained TS tools are bound
but no compiler/build is dispatched. Source-built copies actual freshly admitted
StageA dist/metadata (NOT tar-renamed source). npm install scripts-disabled uses
fixed package, cache/home/config and pinned tools; no ambient configuration or
network authority. Installed directory is physically renamed before moved run.
Product archive is exact-size/hash admitted before same-buffer bounded gunzip;
tar checks framing/member modes/hashes/path domain. Installed/source/moved
package inventory includes unexpected files/directories, not just original paths.

Proposed actual budget30min inclusive,27 active+3 publication;32 known OS starts,
4 supervised children/peak3; install120s/layout420s/case30s/cleanup5s,
64MiB capture total,768MiB work. No automatic retry on deadline/capture/integrity
or unknown retirement. Supervisor captures before spawn, awaits exit/close and
checks owned group absence, TERM then KILL if needed. This inherits StageA's
bounded observer contract, not a kernel-wide drain or arbitrary observer-fault
proof. No unowned kill. Ordinary assertions are rows with child exit0 so all39
can aggregate after safe cleanup; cleanup/deadline aborts dependent roles.

Preparation controls are DATA-only: both exact positive tuple reads, swapped
locators refuse BEFORE open, wrong size before open, wrong hash refuses. No
harmless child controller/installation/product/Worker execution has occurred.
Independent preexecution review must inspect actual controller/source guards;
this seal is a code candidate, not proof that every host permission route works.

The complete StageB726 plan is separate. ALL50 Unit2/layout, other retained
sets/types/mutants and five PUBLIC95 workflows remain mandatory and UNRUN.
No 39-call success, should later occur, establishes coherent acceptance.

